tion\n\nWindows 11 - Godot v3.6.dev - GLES3 - Nvidia Geforce GT1030\n\n### Issue description\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5581e37b-7d2e-4fa8-84b2-3ac8a6c71281)\n\nNearly ago i decided to compile 3.6 branch to expose more data to GDScript to work with (i used latest Microsoft Visual Studio). When i compiled the engine, i noticed that selection in editor doesn't work in one scene. I decided to open some other scenes and selecting something in there, and it turned out that selection ended up with crash.\n\nI thought i did something wrong, but all i did is cloning your repo, at this one specific 3.6.stable commit (3.6. seem to have more commits to it related to 3.6.1).\n\nI have to mention that this is not happening with `debug`, only when i compile an optimized build with `release_debug`.\n\nWould you please tell me any possible ways to fix it myself? I'm posting this issue just to ask a question how to do it\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Have MSVC installed\n- Clone 3.6\n- Build the engine\n- Open any scene and select anything in there\n- Notice weird patterns that some things cannot be selected\n- At some point, get a crash that points into this line when `b` is invalid\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNone","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101783/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101783/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null}